  return this.spawnTrafficAt(x,y,dir);
}
return null;
```
Wait for vertical road x = road*CELL, y=along; lane offset applies x: right.x * LANE = -dir.y*LANE. For dir (0,1): right=(-1,0) → x = road*CELL - LANE ✓ (right-hand side moving down = left side of screen... moving down, right is west (-x), yes correct for right-hand traffic).

For horizontal: y = road*CELL + right.y*LANE, x = along. dir (1,0): right=(0,1) → y = road*CELL+LANE ✓.

Node calc: 
```js
const i = Math.round(x/CELL), j=Math.round(y/CELL);
let ni,nj;
if(dir.x>0) ni=Math.floor(x/CELL)+1; else if(dir.x<0) ni=Math.ceil(x/CELL)-1; else ni=i;
if(dir.y>0) nj=Math.floor(y/CELL)+1; else if(dir.y<0) nj=Math.ceil(y/CELL)-1; else nj=j;
```
x may be offset by lane only perpendicular so rounding fine for the other coordinate.

If ni/nj out of 0..GRID, flip dir and recompute. Use helper nextNodeFor(x,y,dir).

```js
