  // "POLICE"
  ctx.save(); ctx.translate(0,0); ctx.rotate(Math.PI/2)? 
```

In local coords x = length, y = width. The car top-down; text rotated along x with `ctx.rotate(0)` reads along x, width 30px, height 6px. At screen, if car points right, text reads horizontally. Fine. `ctx.font='bold 7px system-ui'`, fill white, centered at (-car.l*0.10, 2)? The roof from -0.24L to 0.26L, width 0.72W. White car roof because body. Draw "POLICE" on roof center maybe readable. Light bar at x=+0.12L? Let's align at x= -car.l*0.04? Police light bar typically center. Draw at local coordinates x=-9..9 near center with two 9x8 blocks. Current does that. Make bigger: x=-12..-2 red, 2..12 blue, y=-car.w/2+2 (top side), but placed across width? In top-down, light bar spans across width (y direction), not length. Wait current `roundRect(ctx, -10, -car.w/2+3, 8, 7, 2)`: x -10..-2, y near -car.w/2+3..-car.w/2+10, so a tiny light block at one side of car, not across roof. That's wrong orientation. A light bar should span across car width at a longitudinal position, i.e. x width ~8 (along length), y across width -car.w/2+3 to car.w/2-3. But then red/blue halves left/right? Top-down light bar spans width: red on one side of y (left), blue the other. Draw two rectangles each 6 tall across width:
